      "intent": {
        "task": "Identify all six original signed coefficient triples, including implicit coefficients and absent terms, without first changing the printed equations.",
        "source_solution": "The six (a,b,c) triples in source order are (2,17,3),(5,-9,4),(1,-12,-6),(-1,1,-2),(8,-7,0),(1,0,-81). A leading minus is a=-1; missing terms have coefficient zero. The coefficients belong to the displayed equations, not an equivalent normalized equation. Full pre-option derivation is frozen in solve-notes.md.",
        "unit_reason": "One complete table coherently tests the same coefficient-reading rule across all six equations and retains the signed/implicit/zero boundary cases. It avoids eighteen cell-level clicks. Monic classification is a distinct definition test in the next question.",
        "concept_blocks": [3, 4],
        "limitations": ["Recognizing a completed coefficient table does not demonstrate independently writing out all six triples."],
        "figure_observations": []
      },
      "key": {
        "correct": ["b"],
        "rationales": [
          {
            "option_id": "a",
            "truth": "incorrect",
            "derivation": "Taking the absolute value of every nonzero coefficient produces (2,17,3),(5,9,4),(1,12,6),(1,1,2),(8,7,0),(1,0,81), exactly this table. The signed original coefficients differ in five rows.",
            "misconception": "Discard each printed minus sign while copying coefficient magnitudes."
          },
          {
            "option_id": "b",
            "truth": "correct",
            "derivation": "Read the coefficients of x^2, x, and 1 with their signs. An unnumbered x^2 contributes 1, -x^2 contributes -1, and an absent x or constant contributes 0, yielding all six displayed triples.",
            "misconception": null
          },
          {
            "option_id": "c",
            "truth": "incorrect",
            "derivation": "Retain a but swap the signed x coefficient with the constant in every row: (a,b,c) becomes (a,c,b). This yields each row shown, including T=(8,0,-7) and U=(1,-81,0).",
            "misconception": "Assign the constant to b and the coefficient of x to c."
          },
          {
            "option_id": "d",
            "truth": "incorrect",
            "derivation": "Divide each full equation by its leading coefficient before reading (a,b,c): (a,b,c) becomes (1,b/a,c/a). This yields all shown rows, including S=(1,-1,2), but those are coefficients of changed equations.",
            "misconception": "Report coefficients of equivalent monic equations instead of the equations as written."
          }
