            "derivation": "Read the correct crossing abscissas -1 and 2, then treat the strict signs as inclusive signs and attach the crossings to both comparison sets. Equality at those crossings contradicts both strict comparisons.",
            "misconception": "Convert the visible crossing boundaries into closed endpoints for < and >."
