    {
      "id": "n42-rational-substitution",
      "source_numbers": ["854"],
      "view": {
        "mode": "single",
        "stem": "Find the value of\n\n$$\\frac{(y-x)^2}{x+y}\\div\\left(\\frac{2xy}{y^2-x^2}+\\frac{x}{x+y}-\\frac{y}{y-x}\\right)$$\n\nwhen $x=8.4$ and $y=-0.6$.",
        "figure_ids": [],
        "options": [
          {"id": "a", "text": "$-9$", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "b", "text": "$1/9$", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "c", "text": "$2025/169$", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "d", "text": "$9$", "figure_ids": []}
        ]
      },
      "intent": {
        "task": "Evaluate the complete rational expression at the original signed decimal inputs, respecting the sum in the divisor and the division of fractions.",
        "source_solution": "Let D=y-x and S=x+y. The bracket has numerator 2xy+xD-yS=2xy-x^2-y^2=-D^2 over DS, so it equals -D/S. The whole expression (D^2/S)/(-D/S)=-D=x-y. All original denominators and the divisor are nonzero because D=-9 and S=39/5. Direct substitution gives first fraction 135/13 and bracket terms 28/195,14/13,-1/15, totaling 15/13; (135/13)/(15/13)=9.",
        "unit_reason": "The full expression is one connected simplification and substitution task. A single complete value preserves the original division and all source data; separating fraction terms into individual clicks would break that dependency.",
        "concept_blocks": [],
        "limitations": ["Selecting the final value does not demonstrate independently producing the common-denominator simplification or checking every original denominator."],
        "figure_observations": []
      },
      "key": {
        "correct": ["d"],
        "rationales": [
          {
            "option_id": "a",
            "truth": "incorrect",
            "derivation": "Replace the bracket numerator 2xy-x^2-y^2 by +(y-x)^2 instead of -(y-x)^2. The bracket then incorrectly becomes D/S. Dividing D^2/S by D/S gives D=y-x=-9.",
            "misconception": "Lose the global minus when factoring 2xy-x^2-y^2."
          },
          {
            "option_id": "b",
            "truth": "incorrect",
            "derivation": "Correct substitution gives A=135/13 and divisor B=15/13. Reverse the requested division and compute B/A=(15/13)/(135/13)=1/9.",
            "misconception": "Interchange dividend and divisor when dividing the two evaluated fractions."
          },
          {
            "option_id": "c",
            "truth": "incorrect",
            "derivation": "Correctly evaluate A=135/13 and B=15/13, but multiply without taking B's reciprocal: A*B=(135*15)/(13*13)=2025/169.",
            "misconception": "Replace division by the bracket with multiplication by that same bracket."
          },
          {
            "option_id": "d",
            "truth": "correct",
            "derivation": "The nonzero bracket is 15/13 and the first fraction is 135/13. Dividing cancels their common denominator and gives 135/15=9, also equal to x-y=8.4-(-0.6).",
            "misconception": null
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
